A common Paper 2 question asks for ways of saving cooking fuel. Give practical, specific points:
1. cover pans with well-fitting lids;
2. use a pan whose base matches the size of the burner;
3. use a pressure cooker for foods that take long;
4. once the liquid boils, turn the flame down to simmer;
5. cut food into small pieces, and soak dried beans first;
6. cook several foods in one pot or one oven load;
7. thaw frozen food before cooking;
8. keep burners clean and check for leaks;
9. boil only the amount of water that is needed.
Do not write vague answers such as "use less gas": say how.
